
      <html xmlns:o='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office' xmlns:w='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40'>
      <head>
      <meta charset="utf-8">
      <title>Scientific Document Integration Test Suite</title>
      <style>
        body { font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; line-height: 1.6; margin: 1in; }
        h1 { color: #1e3a8a; font-size: 24pt; border-bottom: 2px solid #1e3a8a; padding-bottom: 6px; }
        strong { color: #111827; }
        blockquote { border-left: 3px solid #cbd5e1; padding-left: 10px; color: #4b5563; margin-left: 0; }
      </style>
      </head>
      <body>
        <h1>Scientific Document Integration Test Suite</h1>
        
        <h2 style="font-size: 18pt; color: #1e3a8a; margin-top: 24pt; page-break-before: always;">Chemistry: Periodic Trends & Structures</h2>
        <div style="font-size: 11pt; color: #333333; line-height: 1.5;">
          <strong>Definition:</strong><br>> Electronegativity is the tendency of an atom to attract shared electron pairs.<br><br><strong>Key Explanation:</strong><br>Periodic trends follow: F > O > N > Cl. Reaction mechanisms involve the transition states of organic molecules.<br><br><strong>Visual Snippet:</strong><br><img src="https://supabase.co/assets/docA-benzene-crop.png" alt="Organic Structure" style="max-width: 500px; display: block; margin: 10px 0;"><br><br>*Source: Chemistry_Notes.pdf (Page 1)*<br><br><strong>Example:</strong><br>> Reaction: C2H5OH + HCl -> C2H5Cl + H2O
        </div>
      
        <h2 style="font-size: 18pt; color: #1e3a8a; margin-top: 24pt; page-break-before: always;">Physics: Derivations & Circuits</h2>
        <div style="font-size: 11pt; color: #333333; line-height: 1.5;">
          <strong>Definition:</strong><br>> Ohm's Law states that current is directly proportional to voltage.<br><br><strong>Key Explanation:</strong><br>The circuit diagram below shows resistors in series where R_total = R1 + R2 + R3.<br><br><strong>Visual Snippet:</strong><br><img src="https://supabase.co/assets/docB-circuit-crop.png" alt="Circuit Diagram" style="max-width: 500px; display: block; margin: 10px 0;"><br><br>*Source: Physics_Notes.pdf (Page 2)*<br><br><strong>Example:</strong><br>> V = I * R
        </div>
      
        <h2 style="font-size: 18pt; color: #1e3a8a; margin-top: 24pt; page-break-before: always;">Mathematics: Calculus & Matrices</h2>
        <div style="font-size: 11pt; color: #333333; line-height: 1.5;">
          <strong>Definition:</strong><br>> A limit is the value that a function approaches as the input approaches some value.<br><br><strong>Key Explanation:</strong><br>The integration by parts formula: Integral of u dv = u*v - Integral of v du.<br><br><strong>Visual Snippet:</strong><br><img src="https://supabase.co/assets/docC-calculus-crop.png" alt="Calculus Formula" style="max-width: 500px; display: block; margin: 10px 0;"><br><br>*Source: Math_Notes.pdf (Page 5)*<br><br><strong>Example:</strong><br>> Matrix A = [[1, 2], [3, 4]]
        </div>
      
        <h2 style="font-size: 18pt; color: #1e3a8a; margin-top: 24pt; page-break-before: always;">Biology: Organelle Structures</h2>
        <div style="font-size: 11pt; color: #333333; line-height: 1.5;">
          <strong>Definition:</strong><br>> Mitochondria are double-membraned organelles responsible for ATP synthesis.<br><br><strong>Key Explanation:</strong><br>The labelled diagram shows outer membrane, inner membrane, cristae, and matrix.<br><br><strong>Visual Snippet:</strong><br><img src="https://supabase.co/assets/docD-mitochondria-crop.png" alt="Labelled Diagram" style="max-width: 500px; display: block; margin: 10px 0;"><br><br>*Source: Biology_Notes.pdf (Page 8)*<br><br><strong>Example:</strong><br>> Cell Respiration cycle
        </div>
      
